<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan sugar output to date below year-ago level.</title>
<headline>Pakistan sugar output to date below year-ago level.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's sugar production had reached 1.675 million tonnes by February 28 compared to 1.966 million tonnes the same time a year ago, the Pakistan Sugar Mills Association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said mills aimed to produce 2.65 million tonnes in 1996/97, compared to 2.47 million in 1995/96 and 3.0 million in 1994/95. Dealers bought 758,554 tonnes, or 45.26 percent, of the production and the remaining 917,396 tonnes was at the mills. --Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
